# Testing and Release

Spec: `docs/context/TESTING_AND_RELEASE.md`.

## Test classes

- Unit: pricing inputs, rounding, sizing, limits, stops, schema validation,
  transitions, reason codes.
- Invariant/property: determinism, no limit bypass through rounding, no
  duplicate or negative reservation, idempotency under duplicate processing,
  stop monotonicity, illegal transitions rejected.
- Contract: recorded and sanitized feed and broker fixtures, serialization,
  producer/consumer compatibility.
- Scenario/failure: stale, missing, duplicate and out-of-order events, clock
  drift, partial fill, reject, unknown submit timeout, amend/cancel race, rate
  limit, disconnect, restart, broker mismatch, storage failure, AI timeout and
  malformed response, kill switch.
- Replay/research: decision-time visibility, costs, slippage, liquidity, roll,
  expiry, corporate actions, point-in-time universe, walk-forward.

## Conventions

- Test boundaries and failure paths, not the happy path.
- Name the safety invariant a test covers in its docstring so coverage of
  `SAFETY_INVARIANTS.md` is auditable.
- Any change touching an invariant requires an explicit failure test.
- Tests run offline and deterministically. No network, no wall clock, no
  ambient randomness; inject `Clock` and `IdFactory`.

## Gates

Never promote while a data-freshness, risk, idempotency, order-state,
reconciliation, protective-exit, audit, restart or kill-switch test fails.
Profitability or win rate alone is never sufficient evidence.
